    question: "Given static and instance members, explain which method can change which values.",
    slug: "java-given-static-and-instance-members-explain-which-method-can-change-which-values-6",
    shortDescription: "Java interview question covering core java.",
    explanation: "Static methods belong to the class itself and can directly access and modify only static members (class-level fields) because static members exist independent of any object instance. Static methods cannot directly access instance (non-static) fields or call instance methods, because at the point a static method runs, no specific object may exist yet. Instance methods, on the other hand, can access and modify both instance members and static members, since an instance method is always invoked in the context of a particular object, and the class (and its static members) is already loaded.",
    sampleAnswer: "Static methods belong to the class itself and can directly access and modify only static members (class-level fields) because static members exist independent of any object instance. Static methods cannot directly access instance (non-static) fields or call instance methods, because at the point a static method runs, no specific object may exist yet. Instance methods, on the other hand, can access and modify both instance members and static members, since an instance method is always invoked in the context of a particular object, and the class (and its static members) is already loaded.",
