    question: "What is Hibernate?",
    slug: "java-what-is-hibernate-8",
    shortDescription: "Java interview question covering hibernate & jpa.",
    explanation: "Hibernate is a popular Object-Relational Mapping (ORM) framework for Java that maps Java classes to database tables and Java object fields to table columns, allowing developers to work with plain Java objects instead of writing raw SQL and JDBC boilerplate. It handles the translation between the object-oriented domain model and the relational database, manages the object lifecycle (transient, persistent, detached states), provides caching (first-level and second-level) to reduce database hits, supports lazy/eager loading strategies, and offers HQL (Hibernate Query Language) as an object-oriented alternative to SQL. Hibernate is the most widely used implementation of the JPA (Java Persistence API) specification.",
