    shortDescription: "Java interview question covering concurrency & multithreading.",
    explanation: "In Spring, asynchronous REST endpoints can be implemented by having the controller method return a DeferredResult, Callable, or CompletableFuture instead of a direct response object. This frees up the servlet container's request-handling thread while the actual work (e.g., a slow downstream call) happens on a separate thread pool, improving throughput under high concurrency. You enable async support with @EnableAsync and annotate the service method with @Async, or directly return a CompletableFuture composed with supplyAsync/thenApply.",
