    explanation: "ORM (Object-Relational Mapping) is a programming technique that maps objects in an object-oriented language to rows in relational database tables, and object fields to table columns, letting developers interact with the database using familiar object-oriented code instead of writing raw SQL. ORM frameworks (like Hibernate, JPA) handle the translation of CRUD operations, manage relationships (one-to-many, many-to-many) as object references, provide caching, and abstract away database-specific SQL dialect differences, though they can introduce their own learning curve and, if misused, cause performance issues like the N+1 query problem.",
